<article class="env-remark" id="0GBG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GBG">Remark <span data-tag="0GBG">87.21.10</span> <span class="named">(Another variant for Noetherian)</span>.</a>  Let $P$ and $Q$ be local properties of morphisms of $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$, see Remark <a href="/tag/0ANI" data-tag="0ANI">87.21.5</a>. We say <em>$P$ is stable under base change by $Q$</em> if given $B \to A$ and $B \to C$ in $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$ satisfying $P(B \to A)$ and $Q(B \to C)$, then $A \widehat{\otimes }_ B C$ is adic Noetherian and $P(C \to A \widehat{\otimes }_ B C)$ holds. Arguing exactly as in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0GBD" data-tag="0GBD">87.21.7</a> we obtain the following statement: given morphisms $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$ of locally Noetherian formal algebraic spaces over $S$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0ANG" data-tag="0ANG">87.21.3</a> hold for $f$ and $P$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0ANG" data-tag="0ANG">87.21.3</a> hold for $g$ and $Q$, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0ANG" data-tag="0ANG">87.21.3</a> hold for $\text{pr}_2 : X \times _ Y Z \to Z$ and $P$. </p>
